# the argument of aristotle-function.md as claude-opus-5-5 read it: check that it says what the text says
# Aristotle's function argument: two rhetorical questions, both arguing by analogy that Man has a work of his own.
# The analogical steps (from craftsmen, and from bodily members, to Man) are never stated as conditionals; I add them as assumptions.
atom	crafts_have_work	carpenter and cobbler have certain works and courses of action
atom	members_have_work	eye, hand, and foot, and generally each of his members, has manifestly some special work
atom	man_has_work	the whole Man, as Man, has some work of his own (is not left by Nature without a work)
P1	S1	crafts_have_work	kind empirical
P2	S1	members_have_work	kind empirical
A1	-	crafts_have_work → man_has_work
A2	-	members_have_work → man_has_work
C	S1	man_has_work	from P1 P2 A1 A2
